Weather and a wind overlay

Open-Meteo, no key. Tapping a spot gives wind with gusts, temperature,
pressure with a three-hour trend, cloud and rain for the hour on the time
cursor, plus a wind strip across the shooting day. Falling pressure is
called out, since that is the front that moves birds.

The wind layer draws a grid of arrows over the view, refetched when the map
settles or the date and hour change. Arrows point the way the wind blows,
length and colour are speed, and the number under each is mph. Forecast
reaches about sixteen days, and the app says so rather than drawing stale
arrows for a date it cannot see.

Also holds its own reference to Leaflet at startup. A stray global named L
would otherwise break the map, which is a silly way to lose a map.

